WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.002
-The president
is still resisting calls

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.203
to release his tax returns

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.172
while complaining
about immigration laws.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.408
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:11.044
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.814
President Trump
has been resisting calls

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.116
for over three years
to release his tax returns.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.785
Last week Trump said he would
love to release them but can't

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:22.822
because of a fake audit
that definitely does not exist.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.725
And he just kept repeating
the same words over and over.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.494
-While I'm under audit,
I won't do it.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.229
If I'm not under audit,
I would do it.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.664
I had no problem with it.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.333
But while I'm under audit,
I would not give my taxes.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.301
There's no law whatsoever.

00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:39.505
Now, I will say this.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.641
I would love to give them,

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.443
but I'm not going to do it
while I'm under audit.

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:45.778
It's very simple.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.780
-Every time Trump
answers a question,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.650
he sounds like a scientist
insisting on giving a TED Talk

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.920
despite a recent
massive head wound.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.189
"A black hole
is a hole that's black,

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:59.625
and it's black because it's
a hole where there's no light,

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.594
because it's black
and it's a hole.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.630
And that's why they call it
a black hole."

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.132
"Dr. Trump, maybe we could
finish this up tomorrow?"

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:10.402
"But I haven't even gotten
to the black hole part yet."

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:13.205
Also, this part right here
is the best part.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:16.542
-Now, I will say this.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:20.480
I would love to give them,
but I'm not going to do it.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.981
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.884
-He tees it up like
he's about to switch gears

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.253
and then just
repeats himself again.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.321
It's like if you ask someone
to marry you

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:31.290
and they said,
"Well, it's awfully soon

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.225
and I'm a little afraid
of commitment,

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:34.527
but I will say this.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.395
No."

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.162
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.162 --> 00:01:40.633
Knowing that the audit excuse
is a transparent lie,

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.435
Trump has, in the last few
months, moved on to a new excuse

00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:45.437
that his tax returns
are too complicated

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:46.873
for people to understand.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.742
That's what he said last year
after Democrats won the midterms

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.611
and gained the power
to request them.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.846
-As I've told you,
they're under audit.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.214
They have been for a long time.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.884
They're extremely complex.
People wouldn't understand them.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.286
They're done
by among the biggest

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.722
and best law firms
in the country.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.890
Same thing with
the accounting firms.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.793
The accountants are a very,
very large, powerful firm

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:10.196
from the standpoint of respect.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.265
A highly respected, big firm.

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:15.300
A great law firm.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.903
You know it very well.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.805
They do these things.
They put them in.

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:22.308
But people don't understand
tax returns,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.011
and it is a very big company,

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.913
far bigger than you
would even understand.

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:30.350
But it's a great company.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:36.022
But it's big and it's complex
and it's probably feet high.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:39.892
-All right, first of all...

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:43.296
I don't want to hear
how big and complex it is

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:47.533
from someone who also says
it's feet high.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:51.070
Second, the only thing harder to
understand than your tax returns

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.538
is that answer.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.874
We need an audit just to figure
out what the hell you're saying.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.443
Like, honestly, please,
what does this mean?

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.245
-A very, very large,
powerful firm

00:03:00.245 --> 00:03:02.615
from the standpoint of respect.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.584
-Why --

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.752
Why does the president
of the United States

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.254
always sound like a spam e-mail

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.589
asking you for your
Social Security number?

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.891
"Hello. I am with a very large,
powerful firm

00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:14.426
from the standpoint of respect.

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:18.598
Will you please send
your bank routing number?"

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.965
For real?

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.568
For real, maybe Congress
would have more luck

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.003
getting his tax returns

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.672
if they just used his syntax
in the request.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:29.074
"Mr. President, some would say
best president,

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:31.244
we're writing to request
your tax returns.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:34.046
Are willing to send truck
to pick up, as they are so big,

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:37.349
massive even, from your many
large and successful businesses.

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:38.651
Wow!

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.886
We realize they will be
very, very too complicated

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:42.221
for us to understand,

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.423
as we are small from
the standpoint of intelligence,

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:46.259
but would be fun to see them."

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.428
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.897
Yeah.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.035
"They make a very good case.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.937
I think we should
send them over."

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:00.272
Now, the law is clear.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.775
Democrats have the power
to request Trump's tax returns,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.211
which they did, and the request
went to the IRS, not Trump.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.579
It's not up to him.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.881
And yet on Sunday, his
press secretary, Sarah Sanders,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.650
insisted Trump
would not turn them over,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.885
and she even took Trump's
argument one step further,

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.087
saying members of Congress
were literally too dumb

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:16.255
to understand them.

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:18.824
-This is all about
political partisanship.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:21.160
-This is a dangerous,
dangerous road.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.629
And, frankly, Chris,
I don't think Congress,

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.532
particularly not this group
of congressmen and -women,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.535
are smart enough to look through
the thousands of pages

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:33.072
that I would assume that
President Trump's taxes will be.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.607
-Okay, now,
this is what she wants.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.741
She's trolling us.

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.209
She wants us to get all mad
and riled up

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.545
and point out all the ways that
Trump is actually the idiot,

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.013
because that's
their only move --

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.748
to just take whatever
we say about Trump

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:43.782
and turn it back on us,

00:04:43.782 --> 00:04:45.384
and we're just too dignified
for that.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:47.453
We will not stoop to her level.
And I'm just kidding.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.522
Here's a bunch of dumb [bleep]
the president's said and done.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:53.092
-Our hope is a word and world.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:57.229
Through their lives
and though their lives.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:05:00.899
They sacrifice every day
for the furniture --

00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:03.403
future of their children.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:07.139
10,000 known or "suspested"
gang members.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:10.509
Nancy Pelosi, or Nancy,
as I call her.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:11.744
-What is that?

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:14.179
What -- What is --
Wait a second.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:15.448
Is that toilet paper?

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:18.083
-It's tremendously big
and tremendously wet.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:20.019
We appreciated very much
Tim Apple.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:23.656
China has total respect
for Donald Trump

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:28.827
and for Donald Trump's very,
very large a-brain.

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:32.197
-"Very, very...

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:35.968
Very, very large a-brain."

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.472
Yeah, no, but we're too stupid
to understand the tax returns

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.340
of someone who's
clearly suffering

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.542
from what's known
in the medical community

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.778
as degenerative
Italian stereotype disease.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.847
He'll start his next
press conference by saying,

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:50.749
"I use-a my very large-a brain-a

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:54.787
to make-a the pizza pie."

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.322
Now, I will concede

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.923
if Sanders is talking about the
Republican members of Congress,

00:05:57.923 --> 00:05:59.625
then, yes, some of them
are not smart enough

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.026
to understand
Trump's tax returns,

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:03.062
like the guy who vaped
during a congressional hearing

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.631
or the guy who brought out
a giant meme of Ronald Reagan

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.833
riding a velociraptor
and holding a machine gun

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.369
or the guy who brought
a snowball onto the Senate floor

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.304
to claim that global warming
isn't real.

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:15.041
But if you compare that
to the Democrats,

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.143
specifically the new class
of freshmen Democratic women

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.811
who took office this year,
it's different,

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:21.213
like California congresswoman
Katie Porter,

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.416
a law professor
and consumer advocate.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:26.018
Earlier this year,
she grilled Trump's pick

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.921
to lead the Consumer
Financial Protection Bureau,

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.155
Kathy Kraninger,

00:06:30.155 --> 00:06:32.658
who has no experience
in consumer protection.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:35.061
Porter specifically asked her
to explain the difference

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.762
between an interest rate
and an APR.

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:38.497
Now, I don't know
the difference.

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.399
I looked it up three times
this morning,

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:41.800
and I still don't remember.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.803
And I can guarantee you
this guy doesn't understand it,

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:46.339
but the director of the bureau

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:49.542
that's in charge of protecting
consumers from predatory lenders

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.177
should absolutely understand it,

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.245
and yet when Porter
asked Kraninger

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:56.416
to explain the difference,
Porter had to explain it to her.

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:58.817
-Could you please explain
to this committee

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:03.856
the difference between
an interest rate and an APR?

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:07.260
-So, the APR
is the extrapolation

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.394
if it were a one-year term.

00:07:09.394 --> 00:07:12.765
-Ms. Kraninger,
the annual percentage rate --

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.567
and I'll be happy
to send you a copy

00:07:15.567 --> 00:07:17.803
of the textbook that I wrote --

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:23.142
explains that the APR is derived
from the finance charge,

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:26.645
the amount financed,
and the payment schedule.

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:31.216
-Damn, she literally pulled out
the textbook she wrote.

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:33.786
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is --

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:41.693
That is every academic's dream.

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:44.963
"You don't know nothing
about monarch butterflies!"

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:47.066
"What? Oh, my God.
Are -- Are you [bleep] serious?

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:51.871
I wrote the book
on monarch butterflies."

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:54.807
While Trump is resisting calls
to release his tax returns,

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:56.842
he's also been suggesting
breaking the law

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.177
when it comes to immigration.

00:07:58.177 --> 00:07:59.912
Now, here's what's going on.
It's very simple.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:01.280
Trump hates the fact
that migrants

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:03.148
can legally come to this country
and seek asylum.

00:08:03.148 --> 00:08:04.617
He's been whining about it
for months,

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:06.185
complaining that migrants
have the right

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.753
to make their case to a judge
in a court of law

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:08.954
with the help of a lawyer.

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:11.056
And he did it on Friday
and yet again today.

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:13.725
-We have to do something
about asylum.

00:08:13.725 --> 00:08:16.194
And to be honest with you,
have to get rid of judges.

00:08:16.194 --> 00:08:18.797
They have to get rid
of the whole asylum system

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:20.166
because it doesn't work.

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:23.101
And, frankly,
we should get rid of judges.

00:08:23.101 --> 00:08:24.703
We have a stupid system
of courts.

00:08:24.703 --> 00:08:26.405
It's the craziest thing
in the world.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:29.475
We then have to ask them
a couple of questions.

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:32.278
Lawyers are telling them
what to say.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:34.580
They read a little page
given by lawyers

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.148
that are all over the place.

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:39.117
You know, lawyers.
They tell them what to say.

00:08:39.117 --> 00:08:40.085
People come in.

00:08:40.085 --> 00:08:41.787
They read a line from a lawyer

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:43.956
that a lawyer hands them out
online.

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:46.925
The asylum laws
are absolutely insane.

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:48.561
They're given a statement
to read

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:50.629
by lawyers that stand there
waiting for them.

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:51.964
Read the statement.

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.432
-I think Trump is just upset

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:55.568
that they can read
prepared statements,

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:58.503
because he can't read
prepared statements.

00:08:58.503 --> 00:09:04.843
Whenever he reads off
a teleprompter, he Magoos it.

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:08.314
So he can't get rid of courts
or judges or lawyers.

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:09.782
So now Trump has moved on
to a new idea,

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.116
and he clearly thinks
this new idea

00:09:11.116 --> 00:09:12.385
is a brilliant
political maneuver

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:13.819
that will turn the tables
on Democrats.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:16.421
Trump said on Friday he wants
to start sending migrants

00:09:16.421 --> 00:09:18.490
to liberal cities
that would welcome them,

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.859
or so-called sanctuary cites.

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:22.294
-We are looking at
the possibility --

00:09:22.294 --> 00:09:25.364
strongly looking at it,
to be honest with you.

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:28.533
California,
the governor wants to have

00:09:28.533 --> 00:09:32.704
a lot of people coming in,
refugees coming in,

00:09:32.704 --> 00:09:34.240
a lot of sanctuary cities,

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.075
so we'll give them
to the sanctuary cities

00:09:37.075 --> 00:09:38.578
maybe to take care of.

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:41.880
We'll bring them
to sanctuary city areas

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:45.951
and let that particular area
take care of it,

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:47.419
and let's see if they're
so happy.

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:48.821
They always say,
"We have open arms."

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.355
They're always saying
they have open arms.

00:09:50.355 --> 00:09:51.590
Let's see if they
have open arms.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.592
-Man, Trump's press conferences
are so crazy,

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:55.027
now the people
standing behind him

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:56.529
have to wear helmets
and harnesses.

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:59.265
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:01.767
"You'll be standing
behind the president."

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.535
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:05.204
So that's your brilliant
chess moves --

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:07.539
to send poor migrant families
fleeing poverty and violence

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:09.408
to cities that actually
want to welcome them.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:11.576
This is one of the
dumbest attempted trolls
I've ever heard.

00:10:11.576 --> 00:10:13.612
We've all --
We're actively volunteering

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:16.315
to take in more refugees,
and Trump is like, "Oh, I know.

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:17.816
I'll let them take in
more refugees.

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:18.850
That will show them."

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.352
It's like if a friend
volunteered

00:10:20.352 --> 00:10:22.221
to pick you up from the airport
and you were like, "Oh, yeah?

00:10:22.221 --> 00:10:23.289
Well, if you're so good

00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:24.623
at picking people up
at the airport,

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:26.491
then why don't you come
pick me up at the airport?"

00:10:26.491 --> 00:10:29.895
And you'd be like, "Okay,
I'll see you at the airport."

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:31.764
Whether it's on immigration
or tax returns,

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.732
there's one consistent theme
in Trump's behavior.

00:10:33.732 --> 00:10:35.534
He just doesn't think
the law applies to him.

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:37.970
The Constitution grants people,
including immigrants,

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.238
certain inalienable rights.

00:10:39.238 --> 00:10:41.039
And it also gives Congress
the power

00:10:41.039 --> 00:10:42.374
to investigate the president.

00:10:42.374 --> 00:10:44.343
But Trump can't seem
to get that through his...

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:45.677
-...a-brain.

00:10:45.677 --> 00:10:47.613
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:49.782
[ Cheers and applause ]

